# 2026-10-31 — GraphDB backend cloisonnement

## Phase 1 — Two-hat type hierarchy over a shared read root

### Context
Design spec `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-31-graphdb-backend-cloisonnement-design.md`.
The graph-database layer had a single abstract base, `GraphDBBackend` (~1228
LOC), conflating the read contract, the write/companion/sync machinery, and
capability flags. Read-only engines inherited a write surface they cannot
honor, and the materialized-vs-no-copy distinction was a runtime flag rather
than a type. Phase 1 introduces the type hierarchy; it is behavior-identical.

### Changes
1. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphBackend.py` (renamed from `GraphDBBackend.py`):
   renamed the base class `GraphDBBackend` → `GraphBackend` (the shared **read**
   root). Removed the three abstract write methods (`create_table`,
   `drop_table`, `insert_triples`) — they now live on the materialized hat.
   Updated the module/class docstrings and the `is_cypher_backend` isinstance.
2. `src/back/core/graphdb/MaterializedGraphBackend.py` (new): hat interface for
   copy-owning engines (Lakebase, Delta `table`, Neo4j). Declares the abstract
   write contract (`create_table` / `drop_table` / `insert_triples`).
3. `src/back/core/graphdb/VirtualBackend.py` (new): hat interface for read-only,
   no-copy pass-through engines (Delta `view`). It omits the write/build/sync
   surface but does **not** hard-disable the companion read flags — companions
   remain an option governed by the existing search-cache UI setting
   (`auto`/`force_on`/`force_off`); concrete virtual stores set `supports_*`
   per the companions they can actually read.
4. `src/back/core/graphdb/__init__.py`: export `GraphBackend`,
   `MaterializedGraphBackend`, `VirtualBackend` (dropped the `GraphDBBackend`
   export — no backward-compat shim per `.cursor/07`).
5. Re-parented the three backends onto the materialized hat:
   `src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/LakebaseBase.py`,
   `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py`,
   `src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jStore.py`.
6. Updated the base-class references in callers/helpers:
   `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaOverviewStats.py`,
   `src/back/core/reasoning/swrl/SWRLEngine.py`, plus docstring/comment
   references in `adjacency.py`, `GraphDBFactory.py`, `_starter_kit/ExampleStore.py`
   (now subclasses `MaterializedGraphBackend`), the Neo4j modules,
   `SWRLFlatCypherTranslator.py`, `SPARQLRuleEngine.py`, and `LakebaseFlatStore.py`.
7. Updated the refactoring guide example in `src/.coding_rules.md` to describe
   the new `GraphBackend` → hats hierarchy.
8. Tests: repointed subclasses/imports/patch-targets to the new names in
   `tests/units/graphdb/test_graphdb_adjacency_contract.py`,
   `test_search_cache.py`, `test_v090_graph_access_backend.py`,
   `test_materialized_inference_purge.py`,
   `tests/units/core/test_graphdb_factory.py`, `test_sql_literal_escaping.py`,
   `tests/units/dtwin/test_digitaltwin_api.py`.
9. Architecture baseline: renamed the oversized-class key
   `GraphDBBackend.py::GraphDBBackend` → `GraphBackend.py::GraphBackend` and
   tightened it to 1170 via the ratchet
   (`tests/units/architecture/baseline.json`).

