## Phase 3a — Capability interfaces + Delta family cloisonnement

### Context
Design spec §4.4. Build / health / object-listing logic was imported directly
from the Delta backend package by ~13 modules outside `back/core/graphdb/`
(`digitaltwin/**`, `api/**`, `settings/graphengine/**`, `graph_analysis/**`,
`reasoning/**`, `registry/schedule/**`, `core/helpers/**`). This step introduces
the three factory-vended capability interfaces and migrates every Delta call
site off `back.core.graphdb.delta.*` (the `simulation/**` package is handled in
a dedicated cross-cutting `GraphSimulation` step; Lakebase and Neo4j follow in
3b/3c). Companion behaviour is unchanged. Behaviour-identical: the Delta impls
delegate to the same `delta.*` source functions, so existing test patch targets
keep working.

### Changes
1. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphBuilder.py` (new): ABC — build / materialize
   contract (relation naming, `materialize_triples`, `materialize_from_view`,
   `apply_data_relation`, `drop_relation`, `count_triples`,
   `execute_query`/`execute_statement`, `build_steps`, `run_triplestore_build`).
2. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphHealthProbe.py` (new): ABC — health / quality /
   UC object-listing contract (`probe_status`, `schema_permission_summary`,
   `fetch_schema_tables`, `group_triplestore_objects`, `group_analytics_objects`,
   `domain_match_key`).
3. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphProvisioner.py` (new): marker ABC (populated in
   the Lakebase step).
4. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaGraphBuilder.py` (new): Delta `GraphBuilder`
   — thin facade over `_table_naming` / `materialize` / `DeltaBase` /
   `DeltaMaterializedStore` / `DeltaTripleStoreBuildPipeline`. Lazy Build-warehouse
   client, injectable for pipelines that already hold one.
5. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaHealthProbe.py` (new): Delta
   `GraphHealthProbe` — facade over `health` / `objects` / `DeltaBase`.
6. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py`: `get_builder` / `get_health_probe` /
   `get_provisioner` accessors. `engine="delta"` forces the Delta facade for the
   Graph-Analytics materialization path (every backend materializes a Delta
   snapshot for analytics).
7. `src/back/core/graphdb/__init__.py`: export `GraphBuilder`,
   `GraphHealthProbe`, `GraphProvisioner`.
8. Migrated Delta call sites onto the factory accessors:
   `reasoning/ReasoningService.py` (materialize inferred → builder),
   `core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py` (naming → builder),
   `digitaltwin/quality/DataQualitySnapshot.py` (DQ snapshot → builder),
   `digitaltwin/TwinAnalytics.py` (analytics client/query → builder),
   `graph_analysis/JobMetrics.py` + `graph_analysis/preflight.py` (snapshot /
   probe → builder), `digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py` (data relation +
   count, shared `_delta_write_builder`), `digitaltwin/build/_databricks_triplestore_build.py`
   (pipeline → `builder.run_triplestore_build`), `api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   (build info + build steps → builder/probe), `registry/schedule/build.py`
   (count → builder), `settings/graphengine/GraphEngineSettings.py` (objects +
   schema permissions → `_delta_health_probe`).
9. Architecture baseline re-tightened via the ratchet; `_BuildPipeline` shrank
   (compacted debug logs + shared builder helper) so it stays under its budget.
10. `tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_analytics.py`: assert the analytics query
    routes through the Build-warehouse client (via the builder) by invoking it,
    instead of comparing callable identity.

