## Graph DB cloisonnement — Phase 3b: Lakebase family behind the capability factory

### Context
Continuation of the backend cloisonnement. Phase 3b vends the Lakebase family
through the same three factory capabilities and migrates every remaining
`back.core.graphdb.lakebase.*` import outside the `graphdb/` package onto the
factory — except `simulation/**`, which is handled in the dedicated
cross-cutting `GraphSimulation` step (Phase 3d). The capability ABCs are now
**markers** (`GraphBuilder` / `GraphHealthProbe` / `GraphProvisioner`): Delta's
and Lakebase's concrete surfaces diverge, so the method set lives on each
concrete impl while the factory vends the right one per backend. Behaviour is
identical — the Lakebase impls delegate to the same `lakebase.*` source
functions, so existing patch targets keep working.

### Changes
1. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphBuilder.py` / `GraphHealthProbe.py`: converted
   from Delta-specific ABCs to capability **markers** (the engine-specific
   method surface moves to the concrete impls).
2. `src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/LakebaseGraphBuilder.py` (new): Lakebase
   `GraphBuilder` — Lakeflow sync-view DDL (`wrap_view_sql_for_lakeflow`,
   `lakeflow_primary_key`, `ensure_uc_schema_for_synced`), naming / resolution
   (`resolve_sync_uc_fallback_catalog`, `resolve_graph_schema`,
   `physical_table_id`, `synced_phy`) and `is_index_row_size_error`. Thin facade
   over `_companion_ddl` / `_sync_uc_schema` / `LakebaseFlatStore` / `LakebaseBase`.
3. `src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/LakebaseProvisioner.py` (new): Lakebase
   `GraphProvisioner` — config/schema validation (`validate_engine_config`,
   `default_schema`, `validate_graph_schema`, `resolve_postgres_database_override`),
   instance provisioning (`default_branch`/`default_capacity`, `provision_steps`,
   `run_provision`) and synced-table control plane (`delete_synced_table`,
   `sync_manager`, `sync_to_dict`, `sync_state`, `sync_pipeline_id`).
4. `src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/LakebaseHealthProbe.py` (new): Lakebase
   `GraphHealthProbe` — vends the `psycopg` driver handle (`psycopg()`) so health
   / settings probes keep their connection orchestration without importing
   `lakebase.pool` directly.
5. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py`: `_builder_engine` maps a domain's
   graph backend to its builder engine; `get_builder` / `get_health_probe` /
   `get_provisioner` now vend the Lakebase impls (`engine="lakebase"` forces them).
6. Migrated Lakebase call sites onto the factory accessors:
   `session/GlobalConfigService.py` (config validation),
   `domain/settings/graphengine/GraphEngineSettings.py` (synced-table delete),
   `domain/settings/graphengine/GraphEngineLakebaseSettings.py` (schema helpers,
   provisioning, synced-state listing, psycopg probes),
   `digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py` (sync view DDL + UC-schema + PK +
   index-error classifier via new `_lakebase_builder`),
   `registry/schedule/build.py` (sync view DDL + UC-schema + PK),
   `digitaltwin/cache/TwinStoreCache.py` (schema/table/sync-UC name resolution),
   `shared/fastapi/health.py` (3 Lakebase psycopg probes).

