## Graph DB cloisonnement — Phase 3c: Neo4j family behind the capability factory

### Context
Continuation of the backend cloisonnement. Phase 3c vends the Neo4j family
through the same three factory capabilities and migrates every remaining
`back.core.graphdb.neo4j.*` import outside the `graphdb/` package onto the
factory — except `simulation/**` (Phase 3d). Behaviour is identical: the Neo4j
impls delegate to the same `neo4j.*` source functions.

### Changes
1. `src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jGraphBuilder.py` (new): Neo4j `GraphBuilder`
   — property-graph naming helpers (`sanitise_label`, `sanitise_ident`,
   `label_from_class_uri`, `reltype_from_predicate`). Facade over `graph_model`
   / `Neo4jWriteOps.sanitise_label`.
2. `src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jProvisioner.py` (new): Neo4j
   `GraphProvisioner` — credential helpers (`password_env`,
   `is_password_from_secret`).
3. `src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jHealthProbe.py` (new): Neo4j
   `GraphHealthProbe` — builds a `Neo4jConnection` from an engine config
   (`connection`) and vends the read / write op wrappers (`read_ops`,
   `write_ops`), so Settings callers keep their Bolt orchestration without
   importing `neo4j.*`.
4. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py`: `get_builder` / `get_health_probe`
   / `get_provisioner` now vend the Neo4j impls for `engine="neo4j"`.
5. Migrated Neo4j call sites onto the factory accessors:
