## Graph DB cloisonnement — Phase 3d: GraphSimulation cross-cutting step

### Context
Final migration step of Phase 3. The `simulation/**` package dispatched across
all three backends (Lakebase overlay union views, Delta UC sandbox store, Neo4j
marker-label isolation) by importing backend classes directly. Phase 3d lifts
those touch-points behind a new factory-vended `GraphSimulation` capability, so
after this step **no module outside `back/core/graphdb/` imports
`back.core.graphdb.{lakebase,delta,neo4j}.*`** — every backend import is now
confined to `GraphDBFactory`. Behaviour is identical.

### Changes
1. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphSimulation.py` (new): capability ABC — sandbox
   write store (`simulation_store`), `__sim_` / `__smu_` naming
   (`sandbox_table_name`, `sim_union_view_name`, `sim_table_name`), Explorer
   union-view lifecycle (`drop_union` / `ensure_union`), `is_native_store`.
   Safe defaults; each backend overrides what it supports.
2. `src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/LakebaseSimulation.py` (new): Lakebase impl —
   facade over `LakebaseSimulationStore` / `LakebaseSimulationUnion` /
   `_companion_ddl`.
3. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaSimulation.py` (new): Delta impl — vends the
   raw `DeltaMaterializedStore` so sandbox writes can't reach the live inferred
   companion.
4. `src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jSimulation.py` (new): Neo4j impl — sandbox
   store is the live store (marker-label isolation).
5. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py`: `classify_store(store)` (store
   instance → backend kind, for sandbox dispatch) and `get_simulation(kind)`
   (vends the impl; accepts `databricks` ≡ Delta).
6. `src/back/core/graphdb/__init__.py`: export `GraphSimulation`.
7. Migrated `simulation/**` call sites onto the factory:
   `simulation/Sandbox.py` (`__new__` dispatch via `classify_store`,
   Lakebase/Delta sandbox stores + union views via the capability),
   `simulation/Simulation.py` (`sandbox_relation` / `explorer_relation`),
   `simulation/Artifacts.py` (sandbox table + union-view names).
8. `tests/units/simulation/test_simulation_core.py`: updated the sandbox
   lifecycle test to set the capability (`_sim`) on the bypassed instance.

