## Graph DB cloisonnement — Phase 4: lock it in (guardrail + docs)

### Context
Final phase. With every backend import confined to `graphdb/` (Phases 3a–3d),
Phase 4 adds the architecture guardrail that **keeps** it that way and updates
the developer-facing docs + starter kit to the new shape (two hats + four
capability interfaces + the import boundary).

### Changes
1. `tests/units/architecture/test_backend_import_boundary.py` (new): AST guardrail
   over `src/` — asserts **no module outside `src/back/core/graphdb/` imports
   `back.core.graphdb.{lakebase,delta,neo4j}.*`**. Zero offenders today (strict
   assertion, no baseline needed); fails CI on any regression.
2. `docs/diagrams/class-hierarchy.mmd`: redrew the Storage/Backend hierarchy —
   `GraphBackend` read root → `MaterializedGraphBackend` / `VirtualBackend` hats;
   Delta split (`DeltaReadStore` → `DeltaMaterializedStore` / `DeltaViewStore`);
   added the four capability ABCs + their per-backend impls and the
   `GraphDBFactory` accessors. `class-hierarchy.png` regenerated from the updated
   `.mmd` source.
3. `docs/backend.md`: renamed `GraphDBBackend` → `GraphBackend`; split stale
   `DeltaFlatStore` references into `DeltaReadStore` / `DeltaMaterializedStore` /
   `DeltaViewStore`; documented the two hats in "The Contract"; added §2.3
   "Capability interfaces & the import boundary"; extended the integration
   checklist with the hat choice, capability impls, and the boundary rule.
4. `docs/architecture.md`: same `GraphDBBackend` → `GraphBackend` and
   `DeltaFlatStore` → `DeltaMaterializedStore` corrections.
5. `src/back/core/graphdb/_starter_kit/README.md`: added hat selection, a
   "Capabilities & the import boundary" section, and the boundary rule.

